@startuml direct-rialto-state-machine
title direct-rialto PlayerStateMachine (direct-rialto/AampPlayerStateMachine.cpp)

[*] --> IDLE

IDLE --> PIPELINE_CREATED : onPipelineLoaded\n(pipeline load() succeeded)
PIPELINE_CREATED --> SOURCES_ATTACHING : onSourceAttaching\n(first source)
SOURCES_ATTACHING --> SOURCES_ATTACHED : onAllSourcesAttached

SOURCES_ATTACHED --> PLAYING : onPlaybackStarted\n(Rialto PLAYING)
SOURCES_ATTACHED --> PAUSED : onPlaybackPaused\n(Rialto PAUSED)
PLAYING --> PAUSED : onPlaybackPaused
PAUSED --> PLAYING : onPlaybackStarted

SOURCES_ATTACHED --> FLUSHING : onFlush
PLAYING --> FLUSHING : onFlush
PAUSED --> FLUSHING : onFlush
FLUSHED --> FLUSHING : onFlush\n(rapid second seek)

FLUSHING --> FLUSHED : onFlushComplete\n(SEEK_DONE, or an early\nexit / timeout of Flush())
FLUSHED --> PLAYING : onPlaybackStarted\n(Rialto PLAYING)
FLUSHED --> PAUSED : onPlaybackPaused\n(Rialto PAUSED)

FLUSHING --> ERROR : onError
note right of FLUSHING
  onStop and onReconfigure are not handled here:
  Stop() and Configure() first wait for the
  flush to end (waitForFlushComplete),
  so they never see FLUSHING.
end note

ERROR --> IDLE : onStop / onReconfigure

state "any other active state" as ACTIVE
note bottom of ACTIVE
  PIPELINE_CREATED, SOURCES_ATTACHING,
  SOURCES_ATTACHED, PLAYING, PAUSED, FLUSHED:
  onStop -> IDLE, onReconfigure -> IDLE,
  onError -> ERROR.
  IDLE: onReconfigure -> IDLE; onStop is ignored.
end note

note as THREADING
  Each event dispatch takes the state machine's mutex,
  so a single call is atomic.  A sequence such as
  "read currentState(), then act" is not.  The one
  sequence that must be atomic, entering FLUSHING after
  waiting for a previous flush, is serialised by the
  player's m_flushCallMutex.  Every transition wakes
  waitForFlushComplete().
end note
@enduml
